# Ansible Vault password file: prevents Git from committing secrets to remote repos.
# Note:
#  - .gitignore only affects Git tracking (prevents remote commits).
#  - AI tools run locally as your OS user (toor, UID 1000 - non-root):
#    * Passive indexing is scoped only to the open workspace.
#    * Active AI agent tools inherit your exact OS permissions: they can read any file
#      accessible to user 'toor' (including outside workspace), but cannot access root-only
#      files (/etc/shadow, /root/) or other users' restricted files.
# Best practices:
#  1. Restrict filesystem permissions (chmod 600 .vault_pass) so only your OS user can access it.
#  2. Store secrets outside the workspace (e.g. ~/.vault_pass) to avoid workspace indexing.
#  3. Keyring variant (Recommended - 0 plaintext files on disk):
#     Store encrypted in OS keyring (`keyring set ansible vault_pass`) and point vault_password_file
#     to an executable script (`keyring get ansible vault_pass`).
.vault_pass

.localstack/
